2026-10-15|Sum of Squares of Distinct Counts of All Subarrays

Question
Given a 0-indexed integer array `nums`, return the sum of the squares of the distinct counts of all non-empty contiguous subarrays.

Approach
1. Initialize the answer to `0`.

2. Consider every possible starting index `i` of a subarray.

3. For each starting index, create an unordered set to track distinct elements.

4. Extend the subarray one element at a time, using an ending index `j` from `i` to `n - 1`.

5. Insert `nums[j]` into the set. The set automatically maintains only distinct values.

6. The current distinct count is `seen.size()`.

7. Add the square of this count to the answer:
   `answer += distinctCount * distinctCount`

8. Repeat until every subarray has been considered.

9. Time complexity is O(n²) on average, assuming constant-time hash set operations.

10. Space complexity is O(n) for the set.

Solution
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

long long sumCounts(vector<int>& nums) {
    int n = nums.size();
    long long ans = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        unordered_set<int> seen;

        for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
            seen.insert(nums[j]);

            long long distinctCount = seen.size();
            ans += distinctCount * distinctCount;
        }
    }

    return ans;
}

int main() {
    int n;
    cin >> n;

    vector<int> nums(n);

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        cin >> nums[i];
    }

    cout << sumCounts(nums) << '\n';

    return 0;
}
```

Example

Input:
```text
3
1 2 1
```

Output:
```text
15
```

Explanation:

There are six non-empty subarrays. Their squared distinct counts are `1, 1, 1, 4, 4, 4`, whose sum is `15`.
